alex: Quick question — seeing sporadic `Unexpected end of JSON input` in our JS SSE client around token refresh + bursty traffic. Error surfaces in production tracebacks (mostly short chunks split mid-object). Posted a minimal repro in PR #4512, but wanted quick eyes before I iterate. Anyone run into this with streaming + auth refresh?

maria: Yep, ran into something similar last month. Usually the root cause is treating raw stream chunks as whole JSON blobs. With SSE you often get `data:` lines split across chunks. You need a streaming reassembler that handles partial lines and the `data:` prefix.

alex: Example of what we currently do (naive):

```js
let buf = "";
evt.on('data', chunk => {
  buf += chunk;
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(buf);
    handle(obj);
    buf = "";
  } catch (e) {
    // waiting for more
  }
});
```

maria: That pattern fails when you get `data: {` in one chunk and "foo": "bar"} in the next. Try using TextDecoder with streaming and a delimiter-aware loop. Quick sketch:

```js
const decoder = new TextDecoder();
let acc = "";
for await (const chunk of sseStream) {
  acc += decoder.decode(chunk, { stream: true });
  let idx;
  while ((idx = acc.indexOf('\n\n')) !== -1) {
    const frame = acc.slice(0, idx).trim();
    acc = acc.slice(idx + 2);
    if (!frame) continue;
    // strip leading "data: " lines and join them
    const jsonText = frame.split('\n').map(l => l.replace(/^data:\s*/, '')).join('');
    try { handle(JSON.parse(jsonText)); } catch (e) { console.warn('partial parse fail', e); }
  }
}
```

kevin: Also consider backpressure control. If your handler can't keep up, buffer growth + auth refresh spikes will eventually lead to OOM or reorder. Two practical options: 1) bounded in-memory queue + `socket.pause()` when queue len > N, resume when drained; 2) apply small per-request concurrency limiter so bursts get shed earlier. For node streams, `readable.pause()` / `readable.resume()` works.

kevin: Another tip: ensure your SSE parser reassembles `data:` lines strictly (multiple `data:` lines can belong to one event) and only JSON.parse once you have the whole event. We also add a max-event-size guard and emit a metric when we drop/skip a malformed event.

alex: Good call. In PR I added a naive queue but didn't wire pause/resume yet. I'll add a max-event-size too. Does anyone have a recommended default for SSE_BUFFER_LIMIT? I was thinking 1MB.

simon: 1MB default seems fine. Please add a unit test in the sse-test harness that emits intentionally split chunks (split inside the JSON token) + token refresh mid-stream. We need that test green before canary push on Friday. Also tag @tayla as reviewer on the PR.

tayla: Happy to review. Quick ask: add a telemetry counter `sse.partial_json_errors` and a debug log that includes the hex of the last 32 bytes of the preceding chunk so we can triage charset/utf8-split issues.

